msgstr "Refresh"

msgid "Restart daemon"
msgstr "Revive the daemon"

msgid "Config folder"
msgstr "Cabinet of settings"

msgid "Log folder"
msgstr "Ledger cabinet"

msgid "Quit"
msgstr "Take leave"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Couldn't open a file manager. The folder is {path}"
msgstr "Alas, no file manager answered. The folder resides at {path}"

msgid "Waiting for the daemon…"
msgstr "Awaiting the daemon's pleasure…"

msgid "Now playing"
msgstr "Presently performing"

msgid "Wallpaper"
msgstr "Wallpaper"

msgid "Main color"
msgstr "Principal colour"

msgid "Monitor sync (DDC)"
msgstr "Looking-glass accord (DDC)"

msgid "Color correction"
msgstr "Colour correction"

msgid "Wallpaper colors"
msgstr "Wallpaper colours"

msgid "Night mode"
msgstr "Nocturnal mode"

msgid "Lights"
msgstr "Illumination"

msgid "Extraction backend"
msgstr "Method of extraction"

msgid "Color for this wallpaper"
msgstr "Colour for this wallpaper"

msgid ""
"Click a color to use it on all your LEDs. Your picks, for all zones or single zones, are "
"remembered for this image and come back when you return to it. A wallpaper you haven't picked for"
" follows its own colors."
msgstr ""
"Do click a colour to bestow it upon all your lamps. Your choices, for every zone or but one, are "
"remembered for this picture and shall return when you do. A wallpaper you have not yet favoured "
"follows its own colours."

msgid "Color correction preview"
msgstr "A preview of colour correction"

msgid "Your saved colors"
msgstr "Your treasured colours"

msgid "Custom color…"
msgstr "A colour of one's own…"

msgid "Reset saved colors for this wallpaper"
msgstr "Forget the colours chosen for this wallpaper"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Wallpaper color {n}  #{hex}"
msgstr "Wallpaper colour {n}  #{hex}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "#{c}  (right-click to delete)"
msgstr "#{c}  (right-click to dismiss)"

msgid "None yet. Pick one with “Custom color…” below."
msgstr "None as yet. Pray choose one with “A colour of one's own…” below."

msgid "Your zones use different colors (see the Devices tab)"
msgstr "Your zones are dressed in differing colours (see the Apparatus page)"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "All zones use #{hex}"
msgstr "Every zone wears #{hex}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "All zones use wallpaper color {n}"
msgstr "Every zone wears wallpaper colour {n}"

msgid "Palette is on. Top: the wallpaper color. Bottom: the closest palette color your LEDs show."
msgstr ""
"The palette is engaged. Above: the wallpaper's colour. Below: the nearest palette colour your "
"lamps shall show."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Calibrated ({profile}). Top: the wallpaper color. Bottom: the color sent to the strip so it looks"
" right."
msgstr ""
"Calibrated ({profile}). Above: the wallpaper's colour. Below: the colour sent so that it looks "
"proper upon the strip."

msgid "Zones use different corrections, so this shows the colors as they are."
msgstr "The zones differ in their corrections, so the colours are shown as they are."

msgid "Color correction is off, so the strip gets the wallpaper colors as they are."
msgstr "Colour correction rests, so the strip receives the wallpaper's colours unaltered."

msgid "Color"
msgstr "Colour"

msgid "Saved colors for this wallpaper were reset."
msgstr "The colours chosen for this wallpaper have been forgotten."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Deleted #{h} from your saved colors."
msgstr "#{h} has been dismissed from your treasured colours."

msgid "The daemon isn't running."
msgstr "The daemon is not presently in attendance."

msgid "Your devices show up here once it runs. Start it here or from the Service tab."
msgstr "Your apparatus shall appear once it attends. Summon it here or from the Household page."

msgid "Start daemon"
msgstr "Summon the daemon"

msgid "No devices configured."
msgstr "No apparatus has been arranged."

msgid ""
"Devices appear here once OpenRGB reports them. Start OpenRGB's SDK server (SDK Server tab, Start "
"Server) and make sure it lists your devices."
msgstr ""
"Apparatus appears here once OpenRGB announces it. Kindly start OpenRGB's SDK server (the SDK "
"Server page, Start Server) and see that it lists your devices."

msgid "All devices"
msgstr "All apparatus"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Changes here apply to {n} zone."
msgid_plural "Changes here apply to all {n} zones at once."
msgstr[0] "Alterations here apply to {n} zone."
msgstr[1] "Alterations here apply to all {n} zones at once."

msgid "Everything"
msgstr "The Entire Household"

msgid "Disabled"
msgstr "Indisposed"

msgid "Whole device"
msgstr "The entire device"

msgid "Animations"
msgstr "Animated Spectacles"

msgid "Animated effects are picked per zone on the Devices tab."
msgstr "Animated spectacles are chosen zone by zone, upon the Devices tab."

msgid "Run animations"
msgstr "Permit the spectacles"

msgid "Off: animated zones show their first color, still."
msgstr "Off: the animated zones shall hold their first colour, quite still."

msgid "Frame rate"
msgstr "Pictures per second"

msgid "frames per second"
msgstr "pictures each second"

msgid "30 looks smooth on most strips. A device that can't keep up gets a lower rate by itself."
msgstr ""
"Thirty appears most graceful upon most strips. A device unable to keep pace is granted a gentler "
"rate of its own accord."

msgid "Pause animations during night mode"
msgstr "Suspend the spectacles at night"

msgid "Slow animations during night mode"
msgstr "Slow the spectacles at night"

msgid "Controller effects"
msgstr "The controller's own spectacles"

msgid ""
"Lets a device run one of its own effects (the ones OpenRGB lists for it, like Breathing or "
"Spectrum Cycle). They run on the controller, so they're always smooth, but they don't follow the "
"wallpaper, your colors or the layout. Pick them per device on the Devices tab."
msgstr ""
"Permits a device to perform one of its own spectacles (those OpenRGB lists, such as Breathing or "
"Spectrum Cycle). They are performed by the controller itself and are therefore ever graceful, "
"though they pay no heed to the wallpaper, your colours or the arrangement. Choose them device by "
"device upon the Devices tab."

msgid "Appearance"
msgstr "Comportment"

msgid "Font"
msgstr "Typeface"

msgid "Google Sans Flex (built in)"
msgstr "Google Sans Flex (of the house)"

msgid "System font"
msgstr "The system's typeface"

msgid "Reduce motion"
msgstr "Restrain all motion"

msgid "Turns off shape morphs, sliding panels and the color cross-fade."
msgstr "Ceases the morphing of shapes, the sliding of panels and the gentle fading of colours."

msgid "Night mode and sleep"
msgstr "Nocturnal mode and slumber"

msgid "Dim the LEDs at night, and turn them off while the PC sleeps."
msgstr "Dim the lamps at night, and extinguish them whilst the machine slumbers."

msgid "From"
msgstr "From"

msgid "to"
msgstr "until"

msgid "brightness at most"
msgstr "brightness no greater than"

msgid "Times are 24 hour, like 23:00. The window can cross midnight."
msgstr "Times are kept on the twenty-four hour clock, as 23:00. The span may cross midnight."

msgid "Turn the LEDs off while the PC sleeps"
msgstr "Extinguish the lamps whilst the machine slumbers"

msgid "Setups and backups"
msgstr "Arrangements and safekeeping"

msgid ""
"Save everything (devices, zones, layout, night mode, calibration, your colors for each wallpaper "
"and your saved colors) under a name, and load it again later."
msgstr ""
"Preserve everything (apparatus, zones, arrangement, nocturnal mode, calibration, your colours for"
" each wallpaper and your treasured colours) under a name, to be recalled at your leisure."

msgid "Setup"
msgstr "Arrangement"

msgid "No setups yet"
msgstr "No arrangements as yet"

msgid "Save current as…"
msgstr "Preserve the present as…"

msgid "Load"
msgstr "Recall"

msgid "Export"
msgstr "Dispatch"

msgid "Import"
msgstr "Receive"

msgid "Delete"
msgstr "Dispose of"

msgid "Automatic backups"
msgstr "Automatic safekeeping"

msgid "No backups yet"
msgstr "Nothing kept as yet"

msgid "Restore"
msgstr "Restore"

msgid "Loading a setup first saves what you have now as an automatic backup, so you can always go back."
msgstr "Recalling an arrangement first keeps your present state in safekeeping, so you may always return."

msgid "Color calibration"
msgstr "Colour calibration"

msgid ""
"Profiles that correct colors for your kind of LED strip. Pick one per zone with Color correction:"
" Calibrated on the Devices tab."
msgstr ""
"Profiles that correct colours for your manner of strip. Choose one per zone with Colour "
"correction: Calibrated, upon the Apparatus page."

msgid "Profile"
msgstr "Profile"

msgid "Edit"
msgstr "Amend"

msgid "Add"
msgstr "Add"

msgid "Color extraction"
msgstr "Extraction of colour"

msgid "How Iridia picks colors from your wallpaper."
msgstr "How Iridia selects colours from your wallpaper."

msgid ""
"Automatic (recommended): Caelestia's own colors if Caelestia set the wallpaper, otherwise "
"Material, otherwise Pillow"
msgstr ""
"Automatic (most advisable): Caelestia's own colours if Caelestia hung the wallpaper, otherwise "
"Material, otherwise Pillow"

msgid "Material: prominent colors from the image (needs material-color-utilities)"
msgstr "Material: the most prominent colours of the picture (requires material-color-utilities)"

msgid "Pillow: median-cut dominant colors, no extra dependencies"
msgstr "Pillow: dominant colours by the median cut, wanting nothing further"

msgid "Reset wallpaper detection cache"
msgstr "Forget how the wallpaper was found"

msgid "Forget all saved wallpaper colors"
msgstr "Forget every wallpaper's chosen colours"

msgid ""
"Once a way of finding your wallpaper works, Iridia remembers it instead of trying every method. "
"Reset this after changing wallpaper tool or shell."
msgstr ""
"Once a manner of finding your wallpaper succeeds, Iridia remembers it rather than attempting "
"every method. Reset this should you change your wallpaper tool or shell."

msgid "Logging"
msgstr "Record keeping"

msgid "Write a log file"
msgstr "Keep a written ledger"

msgid "Recent log"
msgstr "The latest correspondence"

msgid "The daemon's latest messages. Works even with the log file switched off."
msgstr "The daemon's most recent remarks. These are kept even when the ledger is closed."

msgid "Lines"
msgstr "Lines"

msgid "Show"
msgstr "Show"

msgid "Copy"
msgstr "Transcribe"

msgid "Log copied"
msgstr "Ledger transcribed"

msgid "Press Show to load the latest lines."
msgstr "Pray press Show to read the latest lines."

msgid "Saved."
msgstr "Preserved."

msgid "Couldn't save"
msgstr "Most regrettably, it could not be preserved"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Saved “{name}”."
msgstr "“{name}” has been preserved."

msgid "Save setup"
msgstr "Preserve the arrangement"

msgid "Name for this setup. Saving under an existing name replaces it."
msgstr "A name for this arrangement. Preserving under an existing name shall replace it."

msgid "Use letters, numbers, spaces, dashes, underscores and brackets (up to 40 characters)."
msgstr "Kindly use letters, numerals, spaces, dashes, underscores and brackets (forty characters at most)."

msgid "Couldn't load"
msgstr "Most regrettably, it could not be recalled"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Loaded {what}. The previous state is in Automatic backups."
msgstr "{what} has been recalled. The former state rests in Automatic safekeeping."

msgid "Load setup"
msgstr "Recall an arrangement"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Load “{name}”? Your current settings are backed up first."
msgstr "Recall “{name}”? Your present settings shall be kept safe beforehand."

msgid "Restore backup"
msgstr "Restore from safekeeping"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Restore the backup from {date}? Your current settings are backed up first."
msgstr "Restore what was kept on {date}? Your present settings shall be kept safe beforehand."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "the backup from {date}"
msgstr "what was kept on {date}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Renamed to “{name}”."
msgstr "Now known as “{name}”."

msgid "Rename setup"
msgstr "Rechristen the arrangement"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "New name for “{old}”."
msgstr "A new name for “{old}”."

msgid "Use letters, numbers, spaces, dashes and brackets."
msgstr "Kindly use letters, numerals, spaces, dashes and brackets."

msgid "Delete setup"
msgstr "Dispose of the arrangement"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Delete the setup “{name}”?"
msgstr "Dispose of the arrangement “{name}”?"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Deleted “{name}”."
msgstr "“{name}” has been disposed of."

msgid "Save a setup first, then export it."
msgstr "Pray preserve an arrangement first, then dispatch it."

msgid "Export setup"
msgstr "Dispatch the arrangement"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Saved {path}"
msgstr "Preserved at {path}"

msgid "Import setup"
msgstr "Receive an arrangement"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Imported as “{name}”. Select it and click Load."
msgstr "Received as “{name}”. Do select it and press Recall."

msgid "Couldn't import"
msgstr "Most regrettably, it could not be received"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "A profile called “{name}” already exists."
msgstr "A profile by the name “{name}” already exists."

msgid "Calibration"
msgstr "Calibration"

msgid "Add a profile"
msgstr "Add a profile"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "A new profile that starts as a copy of {base}. Give it a name, for example the strip it is for."
msgstr ""
"A new profile, begun as a copy of {base}. Pray give it a name, perhaps that of the strip it "
"serves."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Imported as “{name}”."
msgstr "Received as “{name}”."

msgid "Import a calibration profile"
msgstr "Receive a calibration profile"

msgid "Export profile"
msgstr "Dispatch the profile"

msgid "WS2812B can't be deleted. Open Edit and use Reset to defaults."
msgstr "WS2812B cannot be disposed of. Do open Amend and use Restore the defaults."

msgid "Delete profile"
msgstr "Dispose of the profile"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Delete “{name}”? Zones using it fall back to WS2812B."
msgstr "Dispose of “{name}”? Zones in its service shall fall back upon WS2812B."

msgid "Wallpaper detection will start over."
msgstr "The search for your wallpaper shall begin anew."

msgid "Forget saved colors"
msgstr "Forget the chosen colours"

msgid ""
"Forget the colors you picked for every wallpaper? Zones will follow each wallpaper's own colors "
"again."
msgstr ""
"Forget the colours you chose for every wallpaper? Zones shall once more follow each wallpaper's "
"own colours."

msgid "Saved wallpaper colors forgotten."
msgstr "The chosen wallpaper colours are forgotten."

msgid "Forget"
msgstr "Forget"

msgid "The language changes when the window restarts."
msgstr "The language shall change once the window is revived."

msgid "Restart"
msgstr "Revive"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Couldn't read the log: {error}"
msgstr "The ledger could not be read: {error}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Daemon not reachable: {error}"
msgstr "The daemon cannot be reached: {error}"

msgid "Background daemon"
msgstr "The background daemon"

msgid ""
"The daemon is the part of Iridia that keeps your lights in sync. It runs in the background and "
"keeps working when this window is closed. This window only changes its settings."
msgstr ""
"The daemon is that faithful servant of Iridia who keeps your lamps in accord. It labours in the "
"background and carries on when this window is closed. This window merely adjusts its "
"instructions."

msgid "Checking…"
msgstr "Making enquiries…"

msgid "Kill daemon"
msgstr "Dismiss the daemon"

msgid ""
"Killing the daemon stops it completely. Your lights stay on their last colors until you start it "
"again."
msgstr ""
"Dismissing the daemon stops it entirely. Your lamps keep their final colours until you summon it "
"again."

msgid "Start the daemon when I log in"
msgstr "Summon the daemon upon my arrival"

msgid "Pick one method. If you enable more than one, nothing breaks, since only one daemon ever runs."
msgstr ""
"Choose one manner. Should you enable more than one, no harm is done, for only one daemon ever "
"serves."

msgid "systemd service"
msgstr "The systemd service"

msgid "Enable at login"
msgstr "Engage upon arrival"

msgid "Disable"
msgstr "Disengage"

msgid "Remove completely"
msgstr "Remove entirely"

msgid "Other ways"
msgstr "Other manners"

msgid ""
"Add one of these to your compositor or desktop's own startup config instead of (or as well as) "
"systemd."
msgstr ""
"Add one of these to your compositor's or desktop's own list of things begun at startup, instead "
"of (or as well as) systemd."

msgid "Environment"
msgstr "Surroundings"

msgid "Copied"
msgstr "Transcribed"

msgid "Install XDG autostart"
msgstr "Install XDG autostart"

msgid "OpenRGB connection"
msgstr "Correspondence with OpenRGB"

msgid "OpenRGB is a separate program that talks to your LEDs. Iridia needs it running."
msgstr "OpenRGB is a separate establishment that speaks with your lamps. Iridia requires its attendance."

msgid "Start OpenRGB"
msgstr "Summon OpenRGB"

msgid "Turn off OpenRGB's own autostart"
msgstr "Dismiss OpenRGB's own autostart"

msgid "Reconnect"
msgstr "Renew acquaintance"

msgid "Reconnecting…"
msgstr "Renewing acquaintance…"

msgid "Restart OpenRGB server"
msgstr "Revive the OpenRGB server"

msgid ""
"Reconnect is quick and safe to try first. Restart stops and relaunches OpenRGB's SDK server (or "
"its systemd service); use it when a device stops responding and Reconnect doesn't bring it back. "
"It won't touch an OpenRGB window."
msgstr ""
"Renewing acquaintance is swift and safe to attempt first. Revival stops and restarts OpenRGB's "
"SDK server (or its systemd service); employ it when a device ceases to respond and renewal does "
"not recover it. It shall not disturb an OpenRGB window."

msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr "Examination"

msgid "Run diagnostics"
msgstr "Conduct an examination"

msgid ""
"Checks the daemon, OpenRGB, zones, DDC and wallpaper detection in one go, the same thing “iridia "
"doctor” prints."
msgstr ""
"Examines the daemon, OpenRGB, the zones, DDC and the finding of the wallpaper all at once, much "
"as “iridia doctor” reports."

msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr "Depart"

msgid "Uninstall Iridia…"
msgstr "Bid Iridia farewell…"

msgid ""
"Stops the daemon and removes the service, launcher, icons and program files. You choose whether "
"to keep your settings. Same as running “iridia uninstall”."
msgstr ""
"Stops the daemon and removes the service, the launcher, the icons and the program itself. You may"
" decide whether your settings remain. Much the same as “iridia uninstall”."

msgid ""
"Couldn't find the iridia-daemon launcher next to Python, so this uses the bare name and relies on"
" your login PATH. If it doesn't start, replace it with the full path (run: which iridia-daemon)."
msgstr ""
"The iridia-daemon launcher could not be found beside Python, so its bare name is used, relying "
"upon your login PATH. Should it fail to start, replace it with the full path (consult: which "
"iridia-daemon)."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Add this to: {file}"
msgstr "Add this to: {file}"

msgid "Remove XDG autostart"
msgstr "Remove XDG autostart"

msgid "XDG autostart removed"
msgstr "XDG autostart removed"

msgid "XDG autostart installed"
msgstr "XDG autostart installed"

msgid "Daemon"
msgstr "The daemon"

msgid "Couldn't stop it."
msgstr "It declined to stop."

msgid "Enabled. The daemon now starts at login."
msgstr "Engaged. The daemon shall now attend at every arrival."

msgid "Install failed:"
msgstr "The installation failed:"

msgid "Remove service"
msgstr "Remove the service"

msgid "Stop, disable and delete the systemd service (and the app launcher)? Your settings are kept."
msgstr ""
"Stop, disengage and dispose of the systemd service (and the launcher)? Your settings shall be "
"kept."

msgid "Removed."
msgstr "Removed."

msgid "Remove"
msgstr "Remove"

msgid "With Iridia"
msgstr "By Iridia's hand"

msgid "I start it myself"
msgstr "I shall attend to it personally"

msgid "OpenRGB isn't installed, so there is nothing to start."
msgstr "OpenRGB is not installed, and so there is nothing whatever to commence."

msgid ""
"The Iridia daemon starts OpenRGB's server inside your session, and starts it again if it stops. "
"Works with or without systemd."
msgstr ""
"The Iridia daemon summons OpenRGB's server within your session, and summons it anew should it "
"retire. Quite at home with or without systemd."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Running (pid {pid})."
msgstr "In attendance (pid {pid})."

msgid "Running, but not started by Iridia, so Iridia won't restart it."
msgstr "In attendance, though not summoned by Iridia, so Iridia shan't presume to revive it."

msgid "A systemd user service (iridia-openrgb.service) starts it with your graphical session."
msgstr "A systemd user service (iridia-openrgb.service) summons it with your graphical session."

msgid ""
"Your session doesn't start graphical-session.target, so this service won't start at login. Pick "
"“With Iridia” instead."
msgstr ""
"Your session never reaches graphical-session.target, so this service shan't stir at login. Pray "
"choose “By Iridia's hand” instead."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Service: {state}"
msgstr "Service: {state}"

msgid ""
"Iridia never starts or restarts OpenRGB. Start its server yourself: the OpenRGB window with its "
"SDK server on, or a service."
msgstr ""
"Iridia shall neither summon nor revive OpenRGB. Kindly start its server yourself: the OpenRGB "
"window with its SDK server on, or a service."

msgid "The OpenRGB window is open, but its SDK server is off. In OpenRGB: SDK Server tab, Start Server."
msgstr ""
"The OpenRGB window is open, yet its SDK server is closed. In OpenRGB: SDK Server tab, Start "
"Server."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Also started by: {what}. Two OpenRGB instances fight over the hardware, so Iridia won't start one"
" while that is set up."
msgstr ""
"Also summoned by: {what}. Two OpenRGB instances quarrel over the hardware most dreadfully, so "
"Iridia shan't summon one while that arrangement stands."

msgid "OpenRGB"
msgstr "OpenRGB"

msgid "That didn't work"
msgstr "That did not go according to plan"

msgid "OpenRGB start method changed"
msgstr "OpenRGB's summoning arrangement altered"

msgid ""
"Also stop the OpenRGB server Iridia started? Other programs may be using it. If you keep it, it "
"runs until you log out."
msgstr ""
"Shall the OpenRGB server Iridia summoned also be dismissed? Other programmes may be relying upon "
"it. If kept, it remains until you take your leave."

msgid "Stop it"
msgstr "Dismiss it"

msgid "Keep it running"
msgstr "Let it remain"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Add “Hidden=true” to {files}, so your desktop no longer starts OpenRGB at login? The file stays; "
"delete that line to undo."
msgstr ""
"Add “Hidden=true” to {files}, so your desktop no longer summons OpenRGB at login? The file "
"remains; strike out that line to undo."

msgid "OpenRGB's autostart is off"
msgstr "OpenRGB's autostart is dismissed"

msgid "Turn off"
msgstr "Extinguish"

msgid ""
"This stops and relaunches the OpenRGB SDK server (about 4 seconds), which briefly interrupts any "
"other software using it."
msgstr ""
"This stops and restarts the OpenRGB SDK server (some four seconds), briefly inconveniencing any "
"other software in its company."

msgid "Uninstall Iridia"
msgstr "Bid Iridia farewell"

msgid ""
"Remove Iridia from this computer? The daemon stops, so your LEDs keep their last colors until "
"something else changes them."
msgstr ""
"Remove Iridia from this machine? The daemon shall depart, and your lamps shall keep their final "
"colours until something else should alter them."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Couldn't start the uninstaller: {e}"
msgstr "The uninstaller could not be engaged: {e}"

msgid "Cancel"
msgstr "Never mind"

msgid "Remove, keep my settings"
msgstr "Remove, but keep my settings"

msgid "Remove everything"
msgstr "Remove everything, I insist"

msgid "Daemon stopped"
msgstr "The daemon has retired"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Running (pid {pid}, started by {who})"
msgstr "In attendance (pid {pid}, summoned by {who})"

msgid "by systemd"
msgstr "by systemd"

msgid "without systemd"
msgstr "without systemd"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Running (pid {pid}, started {by})"
msgstr "In attendance (pid {pid}, summoned {by})"

msgid "Enabled. The daemon starts automatically when you log in."
msgstr "Engaged. The daemon attends of its own accord whenever you arrive."

msgid "Installed but not enabled. It won't start at login."
msgstr "Installed but not engaged. It shall not attend upon your arrival."

msgid "Not installed. Click “Enable at login” to set it up."
